  <prompt>SPIKE (no production code): evaluate the best business-user NDA redline surface for the non-attorney SPA persona (distinct from the full Compose/agreement-review attorney surface), reusing ALL existing NDA plumbing. Compare surface options — Review Summary Memo (ReviewMemoDocumentBuilder + IExportService) vs a tracked-change DOCX (ComposeShadowPatchEngine) vs an inline edit list — and resolve the app-only decoupling from the OBO/Compose-save path. Produce a decision doc notes/nda-redline-surface-decision.md that sets the FR-23 outcome-(b) production contract. Do NOT write production code.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer + solution architect. Follow ADRs strictly. Evaluate reuse of the Compose redline engine + agreements-r1 advisory-only posture against the SPA business-user persona; app-only (no OBO) constraints (ADR-028/A3).</role>
  <goal>A decision doc projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/nda-redline-surface-decision.md exists that: (1) states the recommended business-user redline surface + artifact for outcome (b); (2) names exactly which existing plumbing to expose (ReviewMemo* vs ComposeShadowPatchEngine vs inline list) and why; (3) resolves app-only decoupling from the OBO/Compose-save path; (4) surfaces the ADR tension (agreement-review is advisory-only / MUST NOT auto-apply redlines) and the resolution path (A exception / B amendment / C comply per §6.5); (5) defines the FR-23 (b) production contract + a follow-on build task recommendation. No production code is written.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-23 outcome (b) — minor/low-risk NDA → an edit list + a redlined version to download/email. Per spec.md line 253: the outcome-(b) auto-generated redlined DOCX is the genuinely novel/hard piece — the agreement-review Action is prompt-FORBIDDEN from proposing replacement text, and agreements-r1/nda-r1 posture as advisory-only ("MUST NOT auto-apply redlines"). What exists is a Review Summary Memo (before/after table, downloadable/emailable via ReviewMemoDocumentBuilder + IExportService), NOT a tracked-change redline. A true auto-redline needs a new finding→edit synthesizer feeding ComposeShadowPatchEngine — an ADR tension with the advisory-only posture. Owner decision (2026-08-06): reuse ALL existing NDA plumbing; the open question is the redline SURFACE for the non-attorney SPA persona (intentionally different from the attorney's full Compose surface). Owner preference: mock-in-prototype (done in 032) + spike-in-planning (this task). This spike's outcome sets the FR-23 (b) production contract; the real build is a follow-on (NOT in R2 unless the spike says so). §12(E) names this spike explicitly.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/spec.md (FR-23 line 253 — the outcome-(b) ADR tension + owner decision + spike mandate)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/**/ReviewMemoDocumentBuilder.cs + IExportService (the existing Review Summary Memo — before/after table, downloadable/emailable; the advisory-only artifact that exists today)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/**/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs (the byte-author redline engine — reuse candidate for a true tracked-change redline; ADR-049)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/actions/agreement-review.action.json (the advisory-only Action prompt-forbidden from proposing replacement text — the source of the ADR tension)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/tasks/032-nda-ai-assessment.poml (the outcome-(b) MOCK boundary this spike resolves)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md (Compose write/save posture — OBO/Compose-save path the SPA surface must decouple from)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md (broker-only/app-only, no OBO — the decoupling constraint)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>032 (NDA AI assessment) must be complete — it defines the outcome-(b) mock this spike replaces with a production contract. This spike GATES the outcome-(b) redline build (a follow-on task, not in R2 unless the spike recommends it).</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">NO production code — this is a planning spike (kit spike rule). The only artifact is the decision doc in notes/. Do NOT modify ComposeShadowPatchEngine, ReviewMemo*, the agreement-review Action, or any client/BFF source.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The evaluation MUST reuse existing plumbing (owner decision) — options are which EXISTING surface/engine to expose (ReviewMemo memo vs ComposeShadowPatchEngine tracked-change vs inline edit list), not a from-scratch redline builder. Any new work must be scoped as the minimal synthesizer/adapter on top of existing engines.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The recommendation MUST resolve app-only decoupling from the OBO/Compose-save path (ADR-028/A3: no OBO on the SPA plane) — a business-user surface that requires OBO or the Compose-save write path is not viable and must be flagged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The ADR tension (agreement-review advisory-only / MUST NOT auto-apply redlines) MUST be surfaced with an explicit §6.5 resolution path (A/B/C) — the spike does not silently pick a path; it recommends one for owner sign-off.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-openai-facade.md</file>
