  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/nda-redline-surface-decision.md — options, recommendation, app-only decoupling, ADR-tension path, FR-23 (b) production contract, follow-on build recommendation</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the spike completes, when notes/nda-redline-surface-decision.md is read, then it recommends ONE business-user redline surface + artifact for the non-attorney SPA persona and names the exact existing plumbing to expose (ReviewMemo* / ComposeShadowPatchEngine / inline list).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the recommendation, when reviewed, then it resolves app-only decoupling from the OBO/Compose-save path — a surface requiring OBO is explicitly ruled out or flagged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the advisory-only ADR tension, when reviewed, then the doc surfaces it with an explicit §6.5 A/B/C resolution path for owner sign-off (not a silent pick).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the doc, when reviewed, then it defines the FR-23 (b) production contract + a follow-on build-task recommendation (scope + whether it belongs in R2).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no production code is changed — the diff contains only the decision doc + TASK-INDEX/notes updates (no src/** changes).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Spec FR-23 line 253 + §12(E). SPIKE — no production code; the artifact is the decision doc. 032 mocks outcome (b); this spike sets its production contract and gates the real redline build (a follow-on, not in R2 unless the spike says so). Owner preference: mock-in-prototype (done) + spike-in-planning (this).</notes>
